            <ArticleTitle>Prevention and medical management of postherpetic neuralgia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>275-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Postherpetic neuralgia is the commonest complication of shingles, a debilitating disease common in daily clinical practice. Treatment of postherpetic neuralgia is often complicated, with numerous potential options. This review looks at the evidence in support of the more commonly used medical therapies for this challenging condition.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
